{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FlavorDressing.DressedMassFromSubstrateSplit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FlavorDressing.DressedMassFromSubstrateSplit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.FlavorDressing.FlavorDressingFunctor"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FlavorDressing.dressed_mass_from_substrate_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FlavorDressing.dressed_mass_from_substrate_split","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FlavorDressing/DressedMassFromSubstrateSplit.lean#L100-L127","doc":"**Substrate-pure derivation of the dressed-quark mass\nsplitting.**  Combines `prop:flavor-split-substrate` (substrate\nside) with `lem:pair-skein-mass-formula` (Skein side) to\nexpress `μ_d − μ_u` in terms of `M_N` and `q` alone.\n\nStatement: under positive nucleon-mass scale `M_N` and substrate\nparameter `q > 1`, the equality\n\n  `μ_d − μ_u = M_N · substrate_split_factor q`\n\nholds (up to the `O((Δm/M_N)²)` correction absorbed in the\nSkein-side identity), **conditional on** the named hypothesis\n`DressedMassSubstrateSplit F M_N q`, which is where the two\nunformalised upstream lemmas enter.\n\nNot a tautology (the original Gemini #696 finding): the conclusion\nis a substantive equality drawn from the hypothesis class. Not\nunconditional either (the over-correction that followed, and which\nmade the library inconsistent — see the class docstring above): the\nrelation is asserted only for a triple that carries the instance,\nnot for arbitrary `(F, M_N, q)`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:flavor-dressed-mass-from-substrate-split","label":"prop:flavor-dressed-mass-from-substrate-split","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/flavor-dressed-mass-from-substrate-split.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FlavorDressing.DressedMassSubstrateSplit.split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FlavorDressing.DressedMassSubstrateSplit.split","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FlavorDressing/DressedMassFromSubstrateSplit.lean#L98-L98","doc":"The closed form itself: `μ_d − μ_u = M_N · s(q)`, for *this* `M_N`\n(the nucleon-mass scale of *this* dressing `F`) — the content of\n`prop:flavor-split-substrate` combined with\n`lem:pair-skein-mass-formula`, pending Lean formalisations of both. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FlavorDressing.DressedMassSubstrateSplit.q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FlavorDressing.DressedMassSubstrateSplit.q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FlavorDressing/DressedMassFromSubstrateSplit.lean#L93-L93","doc":"The substrate parameter is above the classical point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FlavorDressing.DressedMassSubstrateSplit.M_N_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FlavorDressing.DressedMassSubstrateSplit.M_N_pos","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FlavorDressing/DressedMassFromSubstrateSplit.lean#L91-L91","doc":"The nucleon-mass scale is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FlavorDressing.DressedMassSubstrateSplit.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FlavorDressing.DressedMassSubstrateSplit.mk","kind":"ctor","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FlavorDressing/DressedMassFromSubstrateSplit.lean#L88-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FlavorDressing.DressedMassSubstrateSplit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FlavorDressing.DressedMassSubstrateSplit","kind":"class","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FlavorDressing/DressedMassFromSubstrateSplit.lean#L37-L98","doc":"**External Skein-side hypothesis** (axiomatised).  The\npair-Skein mass formula of `lem:pair-skein-mass-formula`\napplied to the Borromean baryon braids of the proton and\nneutron gives\n\n  `m_n − m_p = (q + q⁻¹)/(q^{1/2} + q⁻^{1/2}) · (μ_d − μ_u)`.\n\nCombined with the substrate identity\n`(m_n − m_p)/M_N = (q-1)² · (1 − q⁻⁴) / 3` (from\n`prop:flavor-split-substrate`), this rearranges to\n`μ_d − μ_u = M_N · substrate_split_factor q`.  The closed-form\nstatement is recorded as this axiom; promoting it to a theorem\nrequires Lean formalisations of both upstream lemmas.\n**This was an `axiom` until 2026-08-08, and it made the library\ninconsistent.** It read\n\n```lean\naxiom dressed_mass_split_substrate_closed_form\n    (F : FlavorDressingFunctor) (M_N q : ℝ) (_hM : 0 < M_N) (_hq : 1 < q) :\n    F.μ Flavor.down - F.μ Flavor.up = M_N * substrate_split_factor q\n```\n\n`F`, `M_N` and `q` are all universally quantified and mutually\nunrelated: nothing ties `M_N` to `F`. The left side is fixed by `F`\nalone, the right side varies freely with `M_N`. Take the constant\ndressing `μ ≡ 1` (the class is trivially inhabited, `μ_pos` is\n`one_pos`), so the left side is `1 − 1 = 0`, and instantiate at\n`M_N = 1`, `q = 2`:\n\n```lean\ntheorem dressed_mass_axiom_is_inconsistent : False := by\n  have h := dressed_mass_split_substrate_closed_form flatF 1 2 one_pos (by norm_num)\n  simp [flatF, substrate_split_factor] at h\n  …  -- √2 + (√2)⁻¹ = 0, false since √2 > 0\n```\n\nThat compiled, with `#print axioms` naming this axiom. Because\n`substrate_split_factor` is a *concrete* strictly-positive expression\nrather than an opaque symbol, the forced `factor = 0` is refutable, so\nthe defect is `False` rather than mere collapse.\n\nWorth noting how it got here: the docstring below records that a review\n(Gemini #696) flagged the downstream theorem as a **tautology**, and the\nrepair was to introduce this axiom. The tautology fix over-corrected into\nunsoundness — the statement stopped being empty by starting to be false.\n\nThe repair is the §3b-cond hypothesis class below, with **no instance**:\nthe relation holds for a *particular* `(F, M_N, q)` — the nucleon-mass\nscale belonging to that dressing — not for arbitrary triples. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FlavorDressing.substrate_split_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FlavorDressing.substrate_split_factor","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FlavorDressing/DressedMassFromSubstrateSplit.lean#L25-L35","doc":"The leading-order substrate factor\n\n`s(q) = (q − 1)² · (1 − q⁻⁴) / 3 · (√q + 1/√q) / (q + 1/q)`\n\nthat multiplies `M_N` to give the dressed-quark splitting at\nsubstrate parameter `q ∈ ℝ`, `0 < q`.  Defined as a function on\n`ℝ` (we are at the archimedean / numerical layer here per\nAGENTS.md §7c). ","signatureChunk":0}]}